(3979223, 561371, 70000, '<td valign="top">listen i have to tell you i stared at this photo for at least five minutes trying to figure out how it was so silky smooth. it looks like a painting!!! this is just beautiful! i love the doggie''s eyes, you did the eyes like you do alot of peoples eyes and i still have no idea how it was done. haha BEAUTIFUL PUPPY! congrats on your top 10 finish!</td>', 'listen i have to tell you i stared at this photo for at least five minutes trying to figure out how it was so silky smooth. it looks like a painting!!! this is just beautiful! i love the doggie''s eyes, you did the eyes like you do alot of peoples eyes and i still have no idea how it was done. haha BEAUTIFUL PUPPY! congrats on your top 10 finish!', '2007-08-08 01:31:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3979226, 563646, 16197, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by shalrath:</b></div><hr/><i> Amazing depth of field, feels like a painting. I keep getting dragged to the spot of black in the whiskers, you can clone this out in Advanced Editing. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Since it is a stray, I felt it more natural to leave the mark in the whisker.  Kind of like photographing a street person, one isn''t going to ''clean them up'' in post.  They want to portrait them as is.<br/> <br/>Also same reason I kept most of the body in the image, wanted to show how skinny it is from being stray.  <br/> <br/>I photographed this from inside the house through a dirty window L()L.  She was trying to catch birds and climb the tree.  She started moving towards the house than heard the click of the shutter and looked right at me for a couple nice shots.<br/> <br/>I did try to feed her, but she never came for the food.  I see her ever couple of weeks or so, so maybe my house is just on a wandering rotation.</td>', 'Originally posted by shalrath: Amazing depth of field, feels like a painting. I keep getting dragged to the spot of black in the whiskers, you can clone this out in Advanced Editing.   Since it is a stray, I felt it more natural to leave the mark in the whisker.  Kind of like photographing a street person, one isn''t going to ''clean them up'' in post.  They want to portrait them as is. Also same reason I kept most of the body in the image, wanted to show how skinny it is from being stray.   I photographed this from inside the house through a dirty window L()L.  She was trying to catch birds and climb the tree.  She started moving towards the house than heard the click of the shutter and looked right at me for a couple nice shots. I did try to feed her, but she never came for the food.  I see her ever couple of weeks or so, so maybe my house is just on a wandering rotation.', '2007-08-08 01:33:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3979229, 559055, 60173, '<td valign="top">This was way under appreciated. It goes right along with the recent threads about how your subject doesn''t have to be in focus. Had everything been in focus, it would be just another flower with a butterfly on it shot. <br/> <br/>This is a very gentle photo. Soft and calm. <br/> <br/></td>', 'This was way under appreciated. It goes right along with the recent threads about how your subject doesn''t have to be in focus. Had everything been in focus, it would be just another flower with a butterfly on it shot.  This is a very gentle photo. Soft and calm.  ', '2007-08-08 01:34:24.000000', NULL, 0),
