(3992000, 557445, 40106, '<td valign="top">look at you girl! pro status.  this could so be an add for lucky jeans.  i especially love that iron backdrop, adds so much to this.  wonderrrrrrFULLL</td>', 'look at you girl! pro status.  this could so be an add for lucky jeans.  i especially love that iron backdrop, adds so much to this.  wonderrrrrrFULLL', '2007-08-13 02:06:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(3992120, 557445, 60862, '<td valign="top">I''m getting a feeling of an ad from the pose, but I''d be curious what you were going for.  They seem to be two pretty people posed in a somewhat awkward way to sell jeans or something.  In other words, for whatever reason, I''m not getting any emotional connection between them.  Aside from that, I''d like to see more light on the dark sides of their faces.  I''m not one of the people who hates shadows, but I really can''t see much.</td>', 'I''m getting a feeling of an ad from the pose, but I''d be curious what you were going for.  They seem to be two pretty people posed in a somewhat awkward way to sell jeans or something.  In other words, for whatever reason, I''m not getting any emotional connection between them.  Aside from that, I''d like to see more light on the dark sides of their faces.  I''m not one of the people who hates shadows, but I really can''t see much.', '2007-08-13 02:37:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(3992158, 557445, 47316, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by levyj413:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m getting a feeling of an ad from the pose, but I''d be curious what you were going for.  They seem to be two pretty people posed in a somewhat awkward way to sell jeans or something.  In other words, for whatever reason, I''m not getting any emotional connection between them.  Aside from that, I''d like to see more light on the dark sides of their faces.  I''m not one of the people who hates shadows, but I really can''t see much. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I was going for an ad look. You can''t see much? Hmm. Perhaps your monitor is dark because I can see both of their faces clearly on the dark and light side.</td>', 'Originally posted by levyj413: I''m getting a feeling of an ad from the pose, but I''d be curious what you were going for.  They seem to be two pretty people posed in a somewhat awkward way to sell jeans or something.  In other words, for whatever reason, I''m not getting any emotional connection between them.  Aside from that, I''d like to see more light on the dark sides of their faces.  I''m not one of the people who hates shadows, but I really can''t see much.   I was going for an ad look. You can''t see much? Hmm. Perhaps your monitor is dark because I can see both of their faces clearly on the dark and light side.', '2007-08-13 02:49:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3992203, 557445, 60862, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by escapetooz:</b></div><hr/><i>I was going for an ad look. You can''t see much? Hmm. Perhaps your monitor is dark because I can see both of their faces clearly on the dark and light side. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Then you succeeded wonderfully! :)  Sorry - I cut my comment short. I can see their faces fine, although I''d like the shadows to be a bit brighter; I meant I can''t see much detail in their hair.</td>', 'Originally posted by escapetooz:I was going for an ad look. You can''t see much? Hmm. Perhaps your monitor is dark because I can see both of their faces clearly on the dark and light side.   Then you succeeded wonderfully! :)  Sorry - I cut my comment short. I can see their faces fine, although I''d like the shadows to be a bit brighter; I meant I can''t see much detail in their hair.', '2007-08-13 03:06:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3992453, 561219, 62187, '<td valign="top">I''m not normally a ''people'' photog either. Nor do I really like to see them in challenges. But, here at DPC - it''s a fact of life. So, I''ve learned to ''like'' them? If it makes you feel better about the ''Speed Challenge - Free Study'', I gave this photo a 9 - it''s a perfect photo. That''s why were here right - to take technically good photos.</td>', 'I''m not normally a ''people'' photog either. Nor do I really like to see them in challenges. But, here at DPC - it''s a fact of life. So, I''ve learned to ''like'' them? If it makes you feel better about the ''Speed Challenge - Free Study'', I gave this photo a 9 - it''s a perfect photo. That''s why were here right - to take technically good photos.', '2007-08-13 05:50:28.000000', NULL, 0),
