(4253995, 563216, 52336, '<td valign="top">Quite perfect... having gone through your portfolio in more detail, this is very evocative of what you do.  Guttural.</td>', 'Quite perfect... having gone through your portfolio in more detail, this is very evocative of what you do.  Guttural.', '2007-11-17 12:08:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4255497, 559378, 10047, '<td valign="top">Awesome contrast and clarity!</td>', 'Awesome contrast and clarity!', '2007-11-18 13:41:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4257592, 549463, 83313, '<td valign="top">A lot of impact here. To be nitpicky (per your request) the overhead burst and that nicely lit cityscape seem to be fighting for my attention. Perhaps a different crop would clear up what the subject is and lead the eye better.</td>', 'A lot of impact here. To be nitpicky (per your request) the overhead burst and that nicely lit cityscape seem to be fighting for my attention. Perhaps a different crop would clear up what the subject is and lead the eye better.', '2007-11-19 09:32:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4260641, 549463, 60173, '<td valign="top">I have to admit, this photo was the first to jump off the screen. Like everyone else I said "ooo pretty pink." (I hate pink, mind you)<br/> <br/>1) I cropped out the blacker bit of sky in your top left corner. To me this image is about the pink water. Sure, the firework is pretty, but we''ve all seen fireworks, and they themselves don''t have a "wow" factor. With that in mind, it doesn''t hurt to chop a little bit of it out. <br/> <br/>2) I used the Sharpen Tool on your foreground boat. <br/> <br/>3) I Dodged Highlights and Burned Shadows. I find that this helps sharpen images without actually using any of the sharpening tools. It also helps with fog/haze. I used it to bring out your city a bit. I also used it on the main boat to clear it up.<br/> <br/>4) If I could I would move your foremost boat, but I can''t, heh. Composition wise, it needs to be at least 1/2 inch to the left.<br/> <br/>My Edit<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=615115" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/60173/120/615115.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/60173/120/615115.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/60173/120/615115.jpg"/></a></td>', 'I have to admit, this photo was the first to jump off the screen. Like everyone else I said "ooo pretty pink." (I hate pink, mind you) 1) I cropped out the blacker bit of sky in your top left corner. To me this image is about the pink water. Sure, the firework is pretty, but we''ve all seen fireworks, and they themselves don''t have a "wow" factor. With that in mind, it doesn''t hurt to chop a little bit of it out.  2) I used the Sharpen Tool on your foreground boat.  3) I Dodged Highlights and Burned Shadows. I find that this helps sharpen images without actually using any of the sharpening tools. It also helps with fog/haze. I used it to bring out your city a bit. I also used it on the main boat to clear it up. 4) If I could I would move your foremost boat, but I can''t, heh. Composition wise, it needs to be at least 1/2 inch to the left. My Edit', '2007-11-20 15:00:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4260672, 549463, 41098, '<td valign="top">I would add a black border to tie all the crazyness in a bit - overall I think its a great capture.</td>', 'I would add a black border to tie all the crazyness in a bit - overall I think its a great capture.', '2007-11-20 15:12:37.000000', NULL, 0),
